  m_text: An ionic bond forms when electrons are transferred from one atom to another,
    producing oppositely charged ions. In sodium chloride formation, a sodium atom
    transfers one electron to a chlorine atom. Sodium becomes a positively charged
    sodium ion (Na+), while chlorine becomes a negatively charged chloride ion (Cl-).
    The oppositely charged ions attract each other strongly through electrostatic
    forces and form a repeating crystal lattice structure, producing sodium chloride
    (NaCl).
